  the model in front of a checker, and that state is an ELIMINATION WIDER THAN THE SUM IT CORRECTS:
  two parts whose nameplates are points, and a shared block both count whose size is a range.

    team-a nameplate   10 shifts per week   a point
    team-b nameplate   10 shifts per week   a point
    shared block       [2, 3, 5]            counted by both, its size not known exactly
    fused              [15, 17, 18]         20 less the block

  Subtracting the block bound by bound gives [18, 17, 15], which is not a claim: its low exceeds
  its high. The parts' total has no width for the block to move with, so where the block is
  largest the group holds least, and the only ordered reading pairs the sum's low with the
  block's high. The composed nameplate is filed that way, and it is correct.
-->
